From 9ab3142b706e940e2d3bce0ac33ec8d9a9d9b694 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:40:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover iokit/Kernel/IOAnalytics.cpp

Reconstruct the IOKit analytics unit from the KDK 27.0.1 DWARF and the
RELEASE and kasan vmapple kernels: the IOAnalyticsBoot and
IOAnalyticsPeriodic CoreAnalytics events, the handler entries and their
SLIST heads, and the eight static members of the IOAnalytics class.

initialize() allocates the boot and periodic locks, resets the handler
lists and allocates the one-shot periodic thread call at low priority.
registerBootInfoUpdate() retains a boot handler until completeBoot()
runs, then reports it as unsupported. registerPeriodicInfoUpdate()
retains a periodic handler and schedules the daily tick.
deregisterPeriodicInfoUpdate() unlinks, releases and frees an entry and
cancels the tick when the list empties. completeBoot() collects the
boot record from the handlers, copies it into the CoreAnalytics event,
sends it and releases the handlers. schedulePeriodicUpdate(),
cancelPeriodicUpdate() and sendPeriodic() maintain and run the daily
thread call.

The header gains the event records, the block handler types, the class
declaration and its method prototypes at their reference lines.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
---
 iokit/Kernel/IOAnalytics.cpp | 270 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 iokit/Kernel/IOAnalytics.h   | 112 ++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 334 insertions(+), 48 deletions(-)

